# .helmcheckignore — check-helm-values-keys.sh baseline for apps/vaultwarden
# (guerzon/vaultwarden chart, pinned in kustomization.yaml).
#
# One key path per line; `#` comments and blanks ignored. An entry `a.b`
# acknowledges `a.b` and every key nested under it (`a.b.*`). Suppressed keys
# no longer flag, so future commits surface only NEW unknown keys.
#
# Classification method: `grep -rn '.Values.<key>' apps/vaultwarden/charts/*/`.
# Chart reads it → back-compat-OK (renders fine, just absent from the chart's
# published defaults). Chart never reads it → genuine wrong-key (DROPPED).

# ── Back-compat-OK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The chart's templates DO consume these (via `with`/`range`/`toYaml` over a
# list or empty-dict default); they render correctly. Safe to suppress.
image.extraVars        # _podSpec.tpl: `range .Values.image.extraVars`
podSecurityContext     # _podSpec.tpl: `with .Values.podSecurityContext | toYaml`
securityContext        # _podSpec.tpl: toYaml (accepts any subkey)
resources              # toYaml (accepts any subkey)
strategy.type          # deployment/statefulset: `with .Values.strategy | toYaml`
storage.data           # _pvcSpec.tpl reads .name/.accessMode/.size/.class/.path

# ── KNOWN WRONG-KEYS — value is DROPPED at render (NOT back-compat-OK) ───────
# Acknowledged here ONLY so the hook stays green and flags NEW drift. These are
# TRACKED BUGS: fix the key in values.yaml, then DELETE the line (the script
# nudges on stale entries). Right-hand side = the key the chart actually reads.
replicaCount           # chart reads `.Values.replicas` (our value is ignored; default 1 anyway)
websocketEnabled       # not in chart at all (Vaultwarden websockets are built-in now)
disableAdminToken      # chart uses `adminToken.*` (existingSecret/value); this is a no-op
passwordIterations     # not in chart; PASSWORD_ITERATIONS is not exposed by this chart
logging.level          # chart reads `logging.logLevel` (and logging.logFile)
smtp.fromAddress       # chart reads `smtp.from` — our sender address is currently DROPPED
service.port           # chart hardcodes 443/80 and reads `rocket.port` for targetPort
